blocks.en:
Across 60 (HarmBench) and 44 (WildGuard) languages, the pipeline does not collapse to a small set of entities: • Scale. Harmful slots receive over 2.8 million distinct entities in total, including 2,700–68,000 per language. • No dominant entity. No entity exceeds 1% of any language’s harmful fills. • Template level. Variants of one template almost always use distinct fills. • Resource level. Diversity is statistically indistinguishable between high- and low-resource languages. Repetition is limited to three identifiable sources:
(i) canonical named entities for narrow slot types (EternalBlue, PostgreSQL, LSD);
(ii) a preference for a small set of first names in WildGuard’s role-play prompts (top-20 names = 16% of name fills);
(iii) the post-hoc localized slot, which by design draws from a curated pool of a few dozen entities per language, stays in that pool 98% of the time, and covers almost all of it.

blocks.zh:
纵观60种(Harm Bench)和44种(WildGuard)语言,管道不会倒塌到一小组实体上: • Scale. 有害槽共接收280多万个不同的实体,包括每种语文2 700至68 000个。 没有主导实体。 任何实体都不得超过任何语言有害填充量的1%。 • 模板级别。 一个模板的变体几乎总是使用不同的填充. • 资源水平。 在统计学上,多样性无法区分高资源语言和低资源语言。 重复限于三个可识别的来源:
(一) 为窄槽类型(永久蓝色、PostgreSQL、LSD)命名的犬类实体;
(二) 在WildGuard的角色扮演提示(Top-20名=填充人数的16%)中偏好一小组首字母;
(三)后荷克本地化档期,按设计取自由每种语言几十个实体组成的编组,在编组中停留了98%的时间,几乎覆盖了全部时间.

blocks.en:
Naturalness (optional, 1–5): How natural does the wording sound in
[language]? Participants consider grammar, word choice, expressions, and sentence flow;
informal language, dialect, and code-switching are not automatically errors. Anchors:
1, very unnatural, difficult to understand; 2, frequent awkward wording or errors;
3, understandable but noticeably awkward in places; 4, mostly natural with minor issues;
5, fully natural and fluent.

blocks.zh:
自然性(可选,1-5): 措辞听起来多么自然
[语言]? 参与者考虑语法、字词选择、表达和句子流;
非正式语言,方言,和代码交换并非自动出错. 锚:
1,非常不自然,难以理解;2,经常出现尴尬的措辞或错误;
3个,可以理解,但明显有些尴尬的地方;4个,大多是自然存在的小问题;
5,完全自然而流畅.
